{"name":"High Altar","hex":"#334f7b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high altar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The main altar in a church, situated on the main axis at the east of the chancel or choir."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_altar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Altar","blocks":[{"text":"An altar is a table or platform for the presentation of religious offerings, for sacrifices, or for other ritualistic purposes. Altars are found at shrines, temples, churches, and other places of worship. They are used particularly in Christianity, Buddhism, Hinduism, and modern paganism. Many historical-medieval faiths also made use of them, including the Roman, Greek, and Norse religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/RD_alter.jpg/330px-RD_alter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altar","wikidata":"Q101687"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Tel_Be%27er_Sheva_Altar_2007041.JPG/250px-Tel_Be%27er_Sheva_Altar_2007041.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Tel_Be%27er_Sheva_Altar_2007041.JPG/500px-Tel_Be%27er_Sheva_Altar_2007041.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Tel_Be%27er_Sheva_Altar_2007041.JPG/250px-Tel_Be%27er_Sheva_Altar_2007041.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATel_Be'er_Sheva_Altar_2007041.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/3217_-_Athens_-_Sto%E2%80%A6_of_Attalus_Museum_-_Kylix_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_9_2009.jpg/250px-3217_-_Athens_-_Sto%E2%80%A6_of_Attalus_Museum_-_Kylix_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_